:\ntotal 88\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon   128 Aug 20 04:14 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 6 scheschb amazon 16384 Aug 20 04:15 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  6168 Aug 20 04:10 api.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  3874 Aug 20 04:11 fp.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 15662 Aug 20 04:10 gjk.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  4894 Aug 20 04:14 lib.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 15870 Aug 20 04:10 manifold.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  5868 Aug 20 04:10 math.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  4156 Aug 20 04:10 shapes.rs\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon  3971 Aug 20 04:10 types.rs\n  172 src/api.rs\n   94 src/fp.rs\n  458 src/gjk.rs\n   90 src/lib.rs\n  478 src/manifold.rs\n  210 src/math.rs\n  120 src/shapes.rs\n  166 src/types.rs\n 1788 total\n\n=== c_src untouched ===\n746342394bcbfbe7654cebe4f3d21d4e  c_src/src/lib.c\nbf083e977a0f9e803afb6320279de052  c_src/include/lib.h\n7856754ef47525158a2550699ae845a3  c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n\n=== exported symbols (46) ===\nc22 c23 c2AABBtoAABBManifold c2AABBtoCapsuleManifold c2Absv c2Add c2BBVerts c2CCW90 c2CapsuletoCapsu\nleManifold c2CapsuletoPolyManifold c2CircletoAABBManifold c2CircletoCapsuleManifold c2CircletoCircle\nManifold c2Clampv c2Collide c2D c2Det2 c2Dist c2Div c2Dot c2GJK c2GJKSimplexMetric c2Intersect c2L c\n2Len c2MakeProxy c2Maxv c2Minv c2Mulrv c2MulrvT c2Mulvs c2Mulxv c2MulxvT c2Neg c2Norm c2Norms c2Plan\neAt c2RotIdentity c2Skew c2Sub c2Support c2V c2Witness c2xIdentity omni_manifold ptr_from_parts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zx46haf5u2imjh635w3uu6wnjqwyg4x7fy2vmqsqvvqhmgymctwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What was translated\n\nThe whole library — `c_src/src/lib.c` (933 lines, a stripped-down `cute_c2` 2D collision library) — into 8 Rust modules (1,788 lines) in `src/`. `c_src/` is byte-for-byte untouched.\n\n## Completion gate: ABI\n\n`nm -D` on both `.so` files gives **46 exports each, empty diff in both directions**. The five `static` C helpers (`c2Clip`, `c2SidePlanes`, `c2SidePlanesFromPoly`, `c2KeepDeep`, `c2Incident`) are correctly private in Rust too. No namespace-renaming macros existed in this header, so source names are the linker names.\n\n## Getting bit-exact floats — three non-obvious findings\n\n1. **GCC never inlines these functions.** The C library is built without `-fno-semantic-interposition`, so every public→public call goes through the PLT — `c2Len` literally does `call c2Dot@plt`. LLVM inlined instead, which changed which operand became an instruction's *destination*, and on x86 `addss`/`mulss` return the **destination's** NaN when both operands are NaN. Marking all 46 exports `#[inline(never)]` fixed a whole class of divergences.\n\n2. **GCC's destination choice is per-site and often reversed** from source order. I read it out of the disassembly and encoded it in `src/fp.rs` (`fp::add`/`fp::mul` take the destination first), e.g. `c2Mulvs` vectorises to `mulps` with the *broadcast scalar* as destination, and `c2AABBtoAABBManifold` adds extents as `eB + eA`.\n\n3. **`f32::max`/`min`/`abs` are wrong here** — C's ternaries return the second operand on NaN and pass `-0.0` through unchanged.\n\n## Bugs reproduced, not fixed\n\n`c2MakeProxy` and `ptr_from_parts` have no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case and no `default`; `c2Collide` silently ignores polygons; `omni_manifold` leaks both allocations.\n\n## One thing worth flagging\n\nBecause `c2MakeProxy` writes nothing for polygons, **`c2GJK` reads an uninitialised `c2Proxy` off its own stack on every polygon path** — which includes `omni_manifold` for AABB-vs-capsule. I verified empirically that region is normally virgin zero-fill (the polygon then behaves as a point at the origin), so I zero-initialise to match. But the C library's output there is a function of stack layout, not inputs: **the C `.so` segfaults in roughly a third of runs** on the same input set, purely from ASLR. Rust is stable and never crashes. Whenever the C process completes, output matches byte for byte.\n\n## Verification\n\n~1.51 M records compared as **raw bytes** (so NaN payloads and `-0.0` count), all identical: structured corpus over all 46 symbols, random 32-bit patterns (quiet/signalling NaNs of both signs with random payloads, infinities, signed zeros, denormals), random simplices, GJK with/without transforms and with cache round-trips, poison-filled output structs to catch untouched fields, and 443 K `omni_manifold` calls across all 16 type pairs. `cargo build --release` and `cargo test --release` are clean, no warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1220,"cache_read_input_tokens":258943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1220,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ecbe139-cc95-466f-a484-6c87f6cbd230","uuid":"ee231dcb-097f-44ee-b673-4d03d9be6d62","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:15:49.262Z"}
